records.instructions:
1. Founder decision, recorded as a dated product decision in docs/LAUNCH_DEFINITION_OF_DONE.md:
   - default project visibility ('org' or 'members');
   - the project role set (proposed: lead, author, reviewer, approver, viewer);
   - whether org admins and managers see all projects regardless.
2. Migration (Rule 1). Add migrations/<date>_regulatory_program_members.sql: CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS public.regulatory_program_members with:
   - id uuid primary key default gen_random_uuid();
   - organization_id INTEGER NOT NULL references organizations(id);
   - program_id uuid NOT NULL references regulatory_programs(id);
   - user_id INTEGER NOT NULL references users(id);
   - role text NOT NULL with a CHECK on the decided set;
   - status text NOT NULL default 'active', CHECK in ('invited','active','removed');
   - invited_by INTEGER, reason text NOT NULL, created_at/updated_at timestamptz;
   - UNIQUE(program_id, user_id), and an index on (organization_id, user_id).
   Add a trigger or composite FK asserting regulatory_programs.organization_id = NEW.organization_id. Backfill idempotently with INSERT … SELECT id, organization_id, lead_user_id, 'lead', 'backfill: program lead' FROM regulatory_programs WHERE lead_user_id IS NOT NULL ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING, and assert the row count inside the file. Register it in scripts/db/migration-set.mjs C2C_MIGRATION_FILES immediately after 'migrations/20261012b_regulatory_programs_eu_device_classes.sql' and before UUID_TENANT_ISOLATION_NONPUBLIC, so TENANT_ISOLATION_SWEEP policies it. Run npm run ci:migration-set-order and npm run ci:migration-drop-safety.
3. Service. In server/services/c2c/program-access.ts, add programMemberRole(db, programId, orgId, userId) and canReadProgram(...). Extend canMutateProgram to also admit active members with role lead or author. Keep programInOrganization as the single tenancy answer (ci:program-ownership-single-source must stay green). Replace the 'READ ROUTES ARE NOT GATED' header with the new rule.
4. Enforce reads when visibility is 'members' (non-members get 404, not 403):
   - server/routes/c2c/projects.ts:603 list (add an EXISTS membership predicate) and every /:id read;
   - server/routes/c2c/project-vault.ts reads at :1101 (restrict the org-wide search to readable programs), :1134, :1567, :1647, :1708, :1746, :1793, :2117, :2183, :2281, :2294;
   - the authoring list by client_program_id (server/routes/authoring.router.ts:1421).
5. API. Add POST /api/c2c/projects/:id/members, PATCH …/members/:userId and DELETE …/members/:userId, each requiring a reason and writing writeChainedAuditRow in the same transaction. Rewrite GET /:id/team (projects.ts:1205-1250) to read the table.
6. UI. Replace the placeholder at client/src/concept2cure/v2/surfaces/Projects.tsx:700-715 with a picker over org members (role plus reason). Add add/remove/re-role controls to the ProjectHome team panel.
7. Zero duplication. Retire the integer-id sharing API in the same change: server/routes/concept2cure.ts:1716-2042 and services/project-sharing-access.ts. Name the replacement path (POST /api/c2c/projects/:id/members) and its test in the commit message. First confirm via CAT1-11 that nothing on the integer id-space depends on it.
8. Failing-first tests (tests/db, as app_service with RLS_ENFORCE=on), two users in one org:
   (a) a non-member GET of the project, its Vault and its authoring docs returns 404 under 'members' visibility (red on HEAD: 200);
   (b) a member with the author role can pin evidence (red on HEAD: 403);
   (c) removing a member without a reason returns 400;
   (d) the two-tenant contract stays green.

records.evidenceAtHead:
server/routes/authoring.router.ts:5294-5372 POST /docs/:docId/e-sign:
- checkSigningAuthority(actorId, tenant) at :5311 checks the org role only (server/services/part11/signing-authority-gate.ts:45-55);
- meaning APPROVER sets status APPROVED, approved_at and frozen_at in the transaction (:5368-5373) with no author≠approver check and no review prerequisite.
The same holds for POST /docs/:docId/sign (:7373-7420). Why the creator can approve:
- server/middleware/authoringObjectAuthorization.ts:51 classes e-sign as 'approve';
- server/services/authoring/authoring-permissions.ts:88-93: OWNER holds 'approve';
- db/migrations/20260727_authoring_object_permissions.sql:183-216 auto-grants the creator OWNER+AUTHOR;
- a global admin passes outright (authoring-permissions.ts:209);
- createdBy is loaded into scope (:159, :190) but never used in a decision.
The code states the gap itself: server/services/regulatory/authoring-approval-carryover.ts:44-45, 'Authoring approval itself asks for none of this (any signer may approve, with no review)'. The canonical SoD check server/services/governance/separation-of-duties.ts:382 assertSignerIsNotAuthor is not called by authoring.router.ts, and resolveTargetAuthors (:327-364) models no authoring-document target. The client offers Approval to any OWNER/APPROVER holder: client/src/concept2cure/v2/surfaces/AuthoringFilingBar.tsx:135-148. Partial mitigations elsewhere, which leave this route unchanged:
- signing is limited to the admin/approver/reviewer org roles (P-18);
- a Vault lifecycle approval refuses the uploader, sender and reviewer (server/services/regulatory/vault-lifecycle-record.ts:135 SELF_APPROVAL);
- the Authoring→Vault approval carry-over requires reviewer≠approver and neither being the author (authoring-approval-carryover.ts:34-41).
An authored leaf is judged transmittable on status alone (server/services/ectd/leaf-source-resolver.ts:230-238). docs/LAUNCH_DEFINITION_OF_DONE.md P-18 claims 'An author still cannot approve their own document'; the code does not enforce it for Authoring.
